Text File Creation using Python

Aim

To create a text file using Python file handling.

Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4B
- Python 3

Description

The open() function is used to create and open a text file.

- "open("test.txt", "w")" creates a new text file in write mode.
- "f.close()" closes the opened file.

If the file does not exist, Python creates a new file named test.txt.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 make_txtfile.py"

Output

A new file named "test.txt" is created in the current directory.

Conclusion

A text file is successfully created using Python.
